int send_packet(bplid pid, string data) ->
Sends a reliable packet to the specified broadcast pid.
Usually this'll be an ENetPacket.
Called by most of the <a href=send.html>generic send functions</a>.
Returns <samp>&minus;1</samp> if ENet had some sort of error.

int send_packet_unreliable(bplid pid, string data) ->
Sends an unreliable packet to the specified broadcast pid.
Called by send_player_update().
Returns <samp>&minus;1</samp> if ENet was unhappy about that.

int on_any_packet(plid pid, string data) ->
Called when any (ENet) packet is received from the specified pid, regardless of validity.
Returns <samp>0</samp> if the packet is acceptable to use as-is, otherwise <samp>1</samp>.
<!-- TODO: maybe don't return 1, just pipe stuff (const char * and all) directly into on_crap_packet? -->

void on_sane_packet(plid pid, string data) ->
Called when on_any_packet() returns 0.
Calls one of the on_* family of funcs. <!-- TODO: group those together and href to them -->

void on_crap_packet(plid pid, string data) ->
Called when on_any_packet() returns 1.
By default, logs what was wrong with the packet in most circumstances,
and in the case of position, calls send_position() and updates
on_any_packet()'s sanity checkers to account for that.
